	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nh9tvw8Q9RbPkWV_4",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 9, DX 11, IQ 10, HT 10, HP 9, WILL 12, PER 11, FP 10, SPEED 5.25, MOVE 4, DODGE 8, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nMtvnzzZOPEYFzl0Q",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 13 (offense 12, protection 1), threat tier minor, appearing 5."
		},
		{
			"id": "nvJUo_KfR2r9n5j_n",
			"text": "Shortbow: Shortbow (13): 1d+1 impaling, Reach Ranged, 100. Kept behind the door for crows and used, once or twice a generation, for something else. The damage is the bow's."
		},
		{
			"id": "nfCE62BIuv6CwQDaj",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/tallfellow-halfling.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nNoAh4xwsWNpCG2xV",
			"text": "Independent build total: 37 points of racial traits plus 32 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "naNj5IdpQxypZTi54",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Tallfellow Halfling (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nSR2l6RVUXB7IvoQ2",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "niRmk5f9404dtQQ9c",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 45 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "n_OQrJ89kLpqAZ8_i",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 4 (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "n26sYUGYdhekMiK4l",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "nFsr9XSKgns8kUKKE",
			"text": "About 1.2 m standing, which reads nearer the SM -1 row than the -2 row a deep halfling sits on. The difference from its cousins is the whole heading."
		},
		{
			"id": "nQJJT3TGwbe_A10vM",
			"text": "ST 9, one step above the halfling stock, for the same reason: there is simply more of it."
		},
		{
			"id": "nqJC4aHoF8k8XpFty",
			"text": "Acute Vision and Night Vision are what a tallfellow brings that a deep halfling does not. The underground branch buys Dark Vision instead, and neither is a better sense — they are different jobs."
		},
		{
			"id": "nVd9Dd9MLNL0vmUUl",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
